{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Change implemented and committed locally — `5775f968a90` (2026-10-27 ~22:05 PDT)\n\n### Measured first, on `ee5253abfd4`\n\nBuilt the real sdist and listed its top level rather than reading the pattern:\n\n```\n.github  .gitignore  LICENSE  PKG-INFO  README.md  docs  examples\nhatch_build.py  pyproject.toml  scripts  src  tests\n```\n\nPer-entry file counts showed the mechanism precisely: `.github` 1 file, `docs` 4, `examples` 2, `scripts` 1 — **each of those entries is nothing but its `README.md`**, admitted solely by the bare depth-agnostic glob. This is broader than the ticket recorded, which named only the `docs/` tree; `examples/` and `scripts/` ship the same way.\n\n### Change\n\n- `include = [\"src/rebar\", \"tests\", \"/README.md\"]`. Rebuilt: the sdist top level is now `src`, `tests`, `README.md` plus hatchling's own additions — `PKG-INFO` and `pyproject.toml` (sdist metadata), `LICENSE` and the single file `docs/licenses/adjective-adjective-animal-LICENSE.txt` (PEP 639 `license-files`, declared in `[project]`), `hatch_build.py` (the `[tool.hatch.build.hooks.custom]` hook), `.gitignore` (hatchling's sdist default). Every surviving entry traces to a declaration, which is what the first acceptance criterion asks for.\n- Corrected the `infra` exclude comment. Its claim that the allowlist already excluded `infra/` was false while the glob was unanchored — `infra/README.md` would have shipped the directory. Same correction applied to the `evals` exclude's rationale and to `test_the_research_corpus_is_excluded_from_both_distributions`'s docstring, which asserted the same mistaken premise.\n- Two new tests in `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` **build the real archives in-process** via `SdistBuilder`/`WheelBuilder` (~5 s each, no isolated env, no network) and assert their top-level entry sets, plus \"no `README.md` outside the root one and the `tests/` subtree\" and the wheel's `{rebar, *.dist-info}`. They build rather than inspect patterns because this defect was invisible to pattern reading: an unanchored entry looks anchored.\n\n### Red then green\n\nWith the bare `\"README.md\"` restored, `test_the_sdist_ships_only_its_allowlist_and_declared_metadata` fails naming `.github`, `examples`, `scripts` as extra entries. With `/README.md` both new tests pass; the file's 9 tests pass. `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green (`mypy`: no issues in 749 source files).\n\n### `file_impact` not yet declared — deliberate, and it affects the close\n\nThe change touches `pyproject.toml` and `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py`. I have **not** recorded that as `file_impact` yet: this ticket carries a plan-review PASS attestation signed with `material-part: file_impact 003ffa614d5e4a28 0`, and declaring file impact is a material edit that would immediately stale it, forcing a fresh billable review before the ticket can close. Whoever closes this should set `file_impact` to those two paths and re-run `review_plan_start` at that point — the cost is unavoidable but is better paid once, at close, than now.\n\n### State\n\nCommitted on branch `bugsweep-c657653d` with the `rebar-ticket:` trailer and DCO sign-off. `make verify` is running; the change is **not** pushed to Gerrit and the ticket stays `in_progress`. Per AGENTS.md it must not close before its change is `Verified +1` and merged."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793163657445521096,"uuid":"efba9cce-df50-4a25-b669-022b00864b52"}